# Live development preview

The owner's VPS is the development environment. A local edit is not done until it is running there so they can judge the result.

- After a source change, sync it to the live development instance and rebuild or restart only the affected container. Consult ignored `AGENTS.local.md` for connection details. Never copy those details into tracked files, commits, or chat.
- Preserve volumes and runtime data. Never reset volumes or bring the stack down with volume wipes.
- Do not commit, push, or open a pull request unless the owner explicitly asks.
- Never copy remote `.env`, compose overrides, databases, or other private runtime files into Git.
